      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALSACE GEM (7) showed good early speed last start on debut but felt the pinch late and finished sixth at Naracoorte. Has been kept fresh with a month between runs, kept up to the mark with a Murray Bridge jumpout. Rates on top. VASILIAS (6) didn't fire a shot first-up in town when sent out huge odds but there's performances littered throughout last campaign that would stack up strongly for this. Willing to give a look with that run under the belt. DEFY GRAVITY (4) improved last start to finish second over 1200m at Quorn. Not a great deal tougher this time and can get off the mark. BREAK THE LINE (1) made progress last time out, finishing second at the end of 1200m at this track after being prominent at the turn. Has further improvement in store and is one of the main winning chances. CAESOUR'S TOMB (2) was better last start at Murray Bridge in what has proven a strong maiden. Gets in light with the 4kg claim and can be kept safe for a minor spot.",
